AcceptanceCriteria.Criterion:
Add the comment-blind red-control validator function assertCaskSignedDigest(source) inside START_BLOCK_RELEASE_GOVERNANCE_TESTS, mirroring the assertGitleaksChecksumContract / assertPublicationNeedsChain precedent (in-memory source string only, no network, no tracked-file edits): it derives the publish-cask slice by splitting the source on /^ publish-cask:/m and asserts, each with a distinct Error message — the slice contains "- name: download signed macOS release artifacts" with "name: mark-macos-arm64-release" and "path: /tmp/release-stage/mark-macos-arm64-release" and no bare path-only download (a with: block in the slice whose declared keys lack name: is rejected); the sidecar is addressed by the explicit assignments CASK_SIDECAR="/tmp/release-stage/mark-macos-arm64-release/Mark_${VER}_aarch64.dmg.sha256" and SIGNED_DMG="/tmp/release-stage/mark-macos-arm64-release/Mark_${VER}_aarch64.dmg" with a fail-closed existence check; no /find /tmp/release-stage[^
]*Mark_\$\{VER\}_aarch64\.dmg\.sha256/ selection and no "| head -1" applied to a sha256 sidecar anywhere in the slice; the coherence demand holds (sha256sum "$SIGNED_DMG" comparison present, BLOCK_RELEASE_CASK_DIGEST_MISMATCH present, exit 1 on the mismatch branch, no /\|\| true|\|\| echo|set \+e/ around the comparison) and the marker-bearing refusal precedes "gh auth setup-git" in the slice (check-then-mutate ordering, mirroring the requireVerifyThenSign index precedent :301-305); and the B2CR-3 policy holds ("Pull the .sha256 sidecar value (NOT recompute) per B2CR-3." still present, the cask write still uses "$SHA256", the COMPUTED value never appears inside a cask-writing construct). All regexes are CRLF-tolerant (?
) because Windows checkouts carry 
.
